Patch 31 -- scan the cull AABB once per buffer write instead of once per draw.

STATUS: REVERTED from production on 2026-08-13. The numbers below are real but
were taken on a single autoloaded corridor route; the player reported the game
"barely works" with this enabled, so the trade is negative on real scenes. The
switch defaults to off. See MGS2_SEPARABLE_FREEZE_CAPTURE_2026-08-12.md section
6l for what the measurement got wrong.

The largest measured win of this work, and it came from the player's own question:
can the emulation layers be reduced for this? Not for the shader link -- that is
inside the native Mali compiler -- but the visibility culler was doing real
arithmetic in emulated x86 on every single tested draw.

MGS2CULL measured 349 tested draws per frame, and each one rebuilt a model-space
AABB by walking every vertex of its range. The 256x4 cache that used to sit in
front of that never hit: 0 of 112800, because its key carried
mgs2_geometry_generation and MGS2 rewrites its vertex buffers every frame. Patch 28
removed it as dead. Re-keying it cannot work either, for the same reason -- the
vertices really are different after every write.

So this stops caching the answer per draw and changes the question instead. Each
buffer keeps ONE conservative box covering every byte it declares valid, built on
the first cull test after a write and reused by every later draw. Invalidated
exactly where mgs2_geometry_generation is bumped.

The box is larger than the exact per-draw box, so it can only fail to cull
something the exact box would have culled. It can never cull something visible,
which is the only direction that matters for correctness. It falls back to the
exact per-draw scan when the valid-range list has overflowed, since then it no
longer describes the whole buffer, and when the stride or position offset differ
from the cached pair.

Measured on the device, identical autoloaded save and identical walk route:

    MGS2_D3D8_CULL_BOX=1     48.68 fps      (cold)
    MGS2_D3D8_CULL_BOX=1     48.39 fps      (hot, 81.7 C, to rule out temperature)
    MGS2_D3D8_CULL_BOX=0     27.92 fps      (hot)
    in production            48.96 fps

+74%, and screenshots of the two arms are indistinguishable: same corridor, same
character pose, same desk, chair, keyboard, monitor and radar. No page faults, no
GL errors.

Known limit, not observed: a scene where one buffer's valid ranges span most of the
level would give a box too large to cull anything, which costs the culler's own
+17.5% while keeping this saving. The failure mode is slower, never wrong, and
MGS2_D3D8_CULL_BOX=0 returns to the per-draw scan in one run.

